### Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF) Sequence Diagram

This sequence diagram illustrates the step-by-step lifecycle of an asynchronous user request from the UI down to the network and back.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant ComposeView as Jetpack Compose Screen
    participant ViewModel as UserProfileViewModel
    participant UseCase as GetUserProfileUseCase
    participant Repository as UserRepositoryImpl
    participant API as Retrofit API

    User->>ComposeView: Tap "Refresh Profile" Button
    ComposeView->>ViewModel: onEvent(RefreshProfile(userId))
    ViewModel->>ViewModel: Emit StateFlow(Loading)
    ComposeView-->>User: Render CircularProgressIndicator
    ViewModel->>UseCase: invoke(userId)
    UseCase->>Repository: getUserProfile(userId)
    Repository->>API: GET /v1/users/{userId}
    API-->>Repository: Return UserNetworkDto JSON
    Repository->>Repository: Map DTO to Entity & Cache in Room DB
    Repository-->>UseCase: Return Result.success(UserDomainModel)
    UseCase-->>ViewModel: Return Result.success(UserDomainModel)
    ViewModel->>ViewModel: Emit StateFlow(Success(user))
    ViewModel-->>ComposeView: Recompose Screen with Profile Data
    ComposeView-->>User: Display Profile Details & VIP Badges
```

